// lysc 0.12.0 (2026-10-14 12:40 build): in a grand staff, a hairpin whose note starts at a moment where
// the other staff starts nothing is drawn from another column, not from its note.
// - Here (right hand resting): bar 2's crescendo on its last note (fis,,16, x 96.15 in the SVG) is drawn
//   from x 4.48, the system's start, to 101.43. Expected: from 96.15.
// - Without the break (one system): the decrescendo on <c, d,>16 (x 22.91) is drawn from 32.86 (the
//   r4 after it, where the right hand's r4 starts) and the crescendo (73.01) from 38.60 (bar 2's start,
//   where the right hand's r1 starts).
// - The right hand with the left hand's rhythm (c'16 … at the same moments): both start at their notes.
// - A single staff (drop rh and grandStaff): right.
// In OmrGen's pieces (seed 7, --marks) the wrong start is a few spaces off: piano006 bar 3 lh
// `gis,8@cresc` drawn from 31.40 for a note at 45.17, piano002 bar 14 lh `fis,,16@cresc` from 50.83,
// its note at 53.55. Found by the OMR (its reader takes a hairpin's left end as its first note), not a request.
octave absolute
time 5/4

part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }

section Piece {
  rh {
    r1 r4 | break
    r1 r4 |
  }
  lh {
    r2. <c d>16@decresc c8 aes16 r4 |
    r16 g16 <d fis a>8 b8 c'16 b16 g4.@!decresc c8 fis,16 e,16 e,16 fis,16@cresc |
  }
}

score {
  grandStaff {
    staff rh "Right"
    staff lh "Left"
  }
}
